    {
      "answer": "Yes",
      "reason_rejected": "This would require the VLT to see through the Earth's curvature (physically impossible for light) or to be pointed at the ground (mechanically restricted and optically unfocused for such targets). The 'devil's advocate' attack on the horizon limit confirms that even the most generous geometric interpretation (including target height) yields a limit of ~530 km, which is still 20x smaller than the actual distance to the mountains."
